{"name":"Yolanda","hex":"#a291ba","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Yolanda","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Spanish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Yolanda"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yolanda (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Yolanda is a female given name from Western Europe and North America, derived from the Greek name Iolanthe meaning \"Violet\". In German and Dutch the name is spoken similarly but traditionally spelled Jolanda and in Italian, Portuguese and Romanian Iolanda. Yolonda is an African-American spelling of the name. The French form is Yolande. Cognates are the Czech and Slovak Jolantha and the Polish Jolanta."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/Yolanda_Adams_2007Feb11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yolanda_(name)"},{"title":"San Anselmo, California","blocks":[{"text":"San Anselmo is an incorporated town in Marin County, California, United States. San Anselmo is located 1.5 miles (2.4 km) west of San Rafael, at an elevation of 46 feet (14 m). It is located about 20 miles (32 km) north of San Francisco. The town is bordered by San Rafael to the east, Fairfax to the west, and Ross to the south. Mount Tamalpais dominates the view to the south. The population was 12,830 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/San_Anselmo_from_Mount_Tam%2C_February_2026.JPG/330px-San_Anselmo_from_Mount_Tam%2C_February_2026.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Anselmo%2C_California"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/San_Aselmo%2C_CA_USA_-_San_Francisco_Theological_Seminary_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/500px-San_Aselmo%2C_CA_USA_-_San_Francisco_Theological_Seminary_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_